A||N||3||polomeno||Does the Chilton manual cover replacing lifters? for an 84 4 banger??||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||08-22-2001||07:07 PM||||Hey all, I just ordered the Chilton manual so i could replace my lifters but it doenst even list "lifter" in the index.. is it covered anywhere in the manual? if so could someoen tell me what page?  or give me some good instruction on replacing the lifters<P>Thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||TONY_C||08-23-2001||08:44 AM||||Changing the lifters is easy on the duke. Remove the valve cover and loosen the rocker arms and remove the push rods being careful to keep all components in the correct order. there is an access plate on the side of the engine, the side facing the trunk, where you can gain access to the lifters. remove the cover and replace the lifters. after putting all the valve train components back on loosely, refer to the manual as to the proper sequence to adjust the valves.  it is really not too difficult a job to do, i had a lifter collapse on me several years ago and it took maybe 3 hours to do the entire job.  of course you have to remove some other stuff to get to the lifter access plate but the job isnt that hard.||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||08-23-2001||09:20 AM||||I believe its under the "push rod" section, but it is in there..jim (2 '84 Indys)||||reg||6
